=== Distance-3 QCA surface code ===

[[n, k, d]] = [[9, 1, 3]]
  data qubits           = 9
  X-stabilizer rank     = 4
  Z-stabilizer rank     = 4
  logical qubits k      = 1

Stabilizer weights (each must be 4 in this layout):
  X-stabilizers: weights = [4, 4, 4, 4]
  Z-stabilizers: weights = [4, 4, 4, 4]

Distance verification:
  logical X = any full row of 3 data qubits (weight 3)
  logical Z = any full column of 3 data qubits (weight 3)
  distance = 3 (minimum logical weight)

Fault-tolerance capability:
  corrects t = (d-1)/2 = 1 arbitrary X or Z error
  corrects 1 arbitrary single-qubit Pauli error

Physical resources:
  total qubits (data + ancilla) = 9 + 8 = 17
  native gates per stabilizer cycle = 4 CZ per ancilla
  total native gates per QEC cycle  = 8 ancillas * 4 = 32 CZ

Logical error rate vs physical error rate:
    p_phys    p_logical   cycles to fail
------------------------------------------
   1.0e-02     1.00e+00                1
   5.0e-03     2.50e-01                4
   1.0e-03     1.00e-02              100
   5.0e-04     2.50e-03              400
   1.0e-04     1.00e-04            10000

Interpretation:
  The MV3 parallel voter is the fault-tolerant building
  block.  4-voter plaquettes are the standard surface-code
  stabilizer measurement.  Combined, this gives a
  distance-3 surface code with p_th ~ 1e-2 -- the same
  threshold as superconducting and trapped-ion platforms.

  Every gate in this code is a QCA-native CZ.
  No non-native operations required.
